From 11bce813bac191bc33dcdc23ace9c7b55b45d390 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: local <local@localhost>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 14:26:49 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 17/18] Tests: import the PYTHONPATH checkout; stricter compare
 and MLP replay checks

- test_greedy_equal.py: Python put the script's own checkout (wt-batch)
  first on sys.path, so the documented wt-dev run imported wt-batch too.
  The script drops that entry before importing (a PYTHONPATH entry for the
  same checkout stays) and exits unless exllamav3 comes from the first
  PYTHONPATH entry. test_gemv32.py gets the same guard.
- test_greedy_equal.py --compare: both files must carry this script's
  prompt set and one non-empty output per prompt, so a truncated or
  mismatched run fails instead of comparing a subset.
- test_gemv32.py BC GatedMLP check: 8 calls per row count, each with its
  own random input, all kept alive, alternating fp32 / fp16 output (eager,
  capture and replay per dtype, interleaved). After the last call, each
  output is checked against the module's eager path on its own input. A
  replay that reads a stale input or writes a stale or wrongly sized output
  now fails; the old identical-input test could not see it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
